<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TC8 §4.3.3.1 ICMPv4_ERROR_03: ICMP error messages are only sent
  about errors in handling fragment zero of fragmented datagrams.
  TESTER sends a 2-fragment sequence (frag 0 with well-formed
  length-12 Timestamp option + frag 1 with malformed length-10
  Timestamp option); a conformant DUT does NOT emit Parameter
  Problem because options on fragments with offset != 0 are never
  parsed per RFC 791 §3.1.

  Body shared with icmpv4_type_04/05/10/16 + icmpv4_error_04/05
  via sce:template. Dispatch narrows to type=12 — same reply type
  the ERROR_02 positive case observes, but here the absence is
  the pass criterion and presence-from-DUT is the fail.

  Rationale for unicast L2 stimulus despite absence shape: keeping
  the L2 envelope symmetric with ERROR_02 ensures any DUT emission
  of Parameter Problem here would be attributable solely to the
  fragment-zero-vs-fragment-nonzero distinction under test, not to
  a PACKET_HOST kernel-gate difference that would otherwise confound
  both-cases-pass readings. See
  `reference_icmp_packet_host_gate.md`.

  No negative smoke row: absence-shape; any expectation flip also
  lands on timeout → fake-positive verdict. Shared limitation with
  TYPE_04/05/10/16 and ERROR_04/05.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
       version="1.0"
       name="icmpv4_error_03"
       datamodel="null"
       initial="listening">
  <sce:use template="../_templates/icmpv4_negative_absence.sce-template.xml"
           fail_reason="dut_sent_parameter_problem_to_fragmented_sequence"/>
</scxml>
